lX\":true,\"columnDefs\":[{\"name\":\"locus\",\"targets\":0},{\"name\":\"cohort\",\"targets\":1},{\"name\":\"status\",\"targets\":2},{\"name\":\"results\",\"targets\":3},{\"name\":\"literature\",\"targets\":4},{\"name\":\"coincide\",\"targets\":5},{\"name\":\"additional\",\"targets\":6}],\"order\":[],\"autoWidth\":false,\"orderClasses\":false,\"orderCellsTop\":true,\"lengthMenu\":[10,20,25,50,100]}},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {.callout-note collapse=\"true\"}\n## How concordance is calculated\n\n`Concordant` = at least one gene in common between the genes that colocalized on this analysis (`genes_significant`) and the union of literature sources (BigBrain eQTL/sQTL, Bellenguez, SingleBrain). `Discordant` = there's literature for the locus, but none of the genes coincides. `Literature only` = the locus was reported before, but nothing reached significance here. `No comparison` = none of the sources covers this locus (includes all 19 new loci from consensus meta-analysis).\n:::\n",
